cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This pilot is a thin layer over Scott Armstrong's MarkovProcess library,
  which did the hard part. If you use it, please cite MarkovProcess (the
  preferred citation below). To refer to the pilot itself, cite this
  repository at commit 05d99d75df8235e79902220f0fe13e07e81867ca, the commit
  its receipts cover; there is no tagged release.
type: software
title: "MarkovProcess consumer pilot: optional stopping for Brownian motion at a truncated exit time"
abstract: >-
  A small Lean 4 project built on Scott Armstrong's MarkovProcess library. It
  proves that Brownian motion started at x in (a, b), stopped at its exit time
  from (a, b) truncated at a deterministic horizon K, has mean x, and that
  MarkovProcess.IsBrownianReal is equivalent to Mathlib's
  ProbabilityTheory.IsBrownianReal.
authors:
